        "original_id": "490900f6-76af-5161-a6ef-0b46841f562c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: NGC 166, PGC 2143\n- People: Francis Preserved Leavenworth, Frank Muller, Ormond Stone\n- Places: Cetus\n- Concepts: spiral galaxies, apparent magnitude, discovery\n\nFacts:\n- NGC 166, also known as PGC 2143, is a spiral galaxy in the constellation Cetus about 2.6 million light-years away with an apparent magnitude of 15.18.\n- Francis Preserved Leavenworth discovered NGC 166 in 1886.\n- Francis Preserved Leavenworth discovered many New General Catalogue objects together with Frank Muller and Ormond Stone.",
