        "text": "Page: NGC 166. Sentence: NGC 166 (also known as PGC 2143) is a spiral galaxy located around 2.6 million light-years away in the constellation Cetus, with an apparent magnitude of 15.18.\nPage: NGC 166. Sentence: It was discovered by Francis Preserved Leavenworth in 1886.\nPage: Francis Preserved Leavenworth. Sentence: He discovered many New General Catalogue objects together with Frank Muller and Ormond Stone.",
